{
    "background_story": "Presley's life was a miracle from the very beginning. Born prematurely at just 24 weeks, she weighed a mere 1 pound 10 ounces and was no larger than a small doll. Doctors gave her a slim chance of survival, but Presley was a fighter. She spent months in the neonatal intensive care unit, surrounded by beeping machines and the devoted care of her medical team. Against all odds, Presley thrived, her tiny body growing stronger with each passing day. As she grew, her parents marveled at her resilience and spirit. Today, Presley is a happy, healthy toddler, a testament to the power of modern medicine and the will to live. Her journey from a fragile, fetal existence to a vibrant, curious child is an inspiration to all who know her.",
